<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 46,437 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 46,437 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 46,437 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 52,315 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			11,676	    7,535</p>
<p>    Import cargo			34,761	   44,780</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, one ship sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, seven ships were expected to sail and nine were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		  8,000	 Shintoku	   16/12</p>
<p>Crude oil		67,000	 Johar		17/12</p>
<p>High speed deisel    65,000	 Keefan		 due</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasan Megah    21/12</p>
<p>Gas oil		  35,000	 Rosebud	    14/12</p>
<p>Palm oil		 18,000	 Wawasan Murni    16/12</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	    5,350	 Champion Trader  19/12</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
